1
00:03:24,324 --> 00:03:30,324
A Spike Jonze love story.

2
00:06:48,648 --> 00:06:54,648
Her is a romance, science fiction, drama film directed by Spike Jonze.

3
00:10:12,972 --> 00:10:18,972
In the not so distant future, Theodore, a lonely writer, purchases a newly
developed operating system designed to meet the user's every need.

4
00:13:37,297 --> 00:13:43,297
To Theodore's surprise, a romantic relationship develops
between him and his operating system.

5
00:17:01,621 --> 00:17:07,621
This unconventional love story blends science fiction and romance in a sweet tale that explores
the nature of love and the ways that technology isolates and connects us all.

6
00:20:25,945 --> 00:20:31,945
Theodore, played by Joaquin Phoenix.

7
00:23:50,270 --> 00:23:56,270
Samantha (voice), played by Scarlett Johansson.

8
00:27:14,594 --> 00:27:20,594
Letter Writer #1, played by Lynn Adrianna.

9
00:30:38,918 --> 00:30:44,918
Letter Writer #2, played by Lisa Renee Pitts.

10
00:34:03,243 --> 00:34:09,243
Letter Writer #3, played by Gabe Gomez.

11
00:37:27,567 --> 00:37:33,567
Paul, played by Chris Pratt.

12
00:40:51,891 --> 00:40:57,891
Her  is a 2013 American science fiction romantic drama film
written, co-produced, and directed by Spike Jonze.

13
00:44:16,216 --> 00:44:22,216
It follows Theodore Twombly (Joaquin Phoenix), a man who develops a relationship with Samantha (Scarlett
Johansson), an artificially intelligent operating system personified through a female voice.

14
00:47:40,540 --> 00:47:46,540
The film also stars Amy Adams, Rooney Mara, Olivia Wilde, and Chris Pratt.

15
00:51:04,864 --> 00:51:10,864
The film was dedicated to James Gandolfini, Harris Savides, Maurice
Sendak, and Adam Yauch, who all died before the film's release.

16
00:54:29,189 --> 00:54:35,189
As of 2026, Her is the most recent narrative film directed by Jonze.

17
00:57:53,513 --> 00:57:59,513
The events of the movie take place in an unspecified near future, in a world where
progress makes life comfortable, but leaves space for a profound loneliness.

18
01:01:17,837 --> 01:01:23,837
Jonze conceived the idea in the early 2000s after reading an article about a website that
allowed for instant messaging with an artificial intelligence program.

19
01:04:42,162 --> 01:04:48,162
After making I'm Here (2010), a short film sharing
similar themes, Jonze returned to the idea.

20
01:08:06,486 --> 01:08:12,486
He wrote the first draft of the script in five months,
marking his solo screenwriting debut.

21
01:11:30,810 --> 01:11:36,810
Principal photography took place in Los Angeles and Shanghai in mid-2012.

22
01:14:55,135 --> 01:15:01,135
The voice of Samantha was recast in post-production, with
Samantha Morton being replaced with Johansson.

23
01:18:19,459 --> 01:18:25,459
Additional scenes were filmed in August 2013 following the casting change.

24
01:21:43,783 --> 01:21:49,783
Her premiered at the New York Film Festival on October 12, 2013.

25
01:25:08,108 --> 01:25:14,108
Following a limited six-theater release that December, Warner Bros.

26
01:28:32,432 --> 01:28:38,432
Pictures wide released Her in over 1,700 theaters in the
United States and Canada on January 10, 2014.

27
01:31:56,756 --> 01:32:02,756
Her received critical acclaim, particularly for the performances of
Phoenix and Johansson, and Jonze's writing and direction.

28
01:35:21,081 --> 01:35:27,081
It grossed over $48 million worldwide on a production budget of $23 million.

29
01:38:45,405 --> 01:38:51,405
The film received numerous awards and nominations,
primarily for Jonze's screenplay.

30
01:42:09,729 --> 01:42:15,729
At the 86th Academy Awards, Her received five nominations, including
Best Picture, and won for Best Original Screenplay.

31
01:45:34,054 --> 01:45:40,054
Jonze also won awards for his screenplay at the Golden Globes, the WGA
Awards, the Critics' Choice Awards, and the Saturn Awards.

32
01:48:58,378 --> 01:49:04,378
In a 2016 BBC poll of 177 critics around the world, Her was
voted the 84th-greatest film since 2000.

33
01:52:22,702 --> 01:52:28,702
Since its release, Her has developed a cult following.

34
01:55:47,027 --> 01:55:53,027
It is now considered to be one of the best films of the 21st century
and one of the best science fiction films of all time.

35
01:59:11,351 --> 01:59:17,351
The film explores themes of future, artificial
intelligence (a.i.), computer, satire, love.

36
02:02:35,675 --> 02:02:41,675
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
